❗ WHY THIS ERROR HAPPENS

You likely did something like:

HeaderContainer.Width = Gallery_Suppliers_New.Width
Gallery_Suppliers_New.Width = HeaderContainer.Width

👉 This creates a loop:

Header → depends on Gallery  
Gallery → depends on Header  
❌ Infinite loop → ERROR


---

✅ SOLUTION: USE ONE SOURCE OF TRUTH

👉 Only ONE control computes the width
👉 Others just follow it


---

🎯 RECOMMENDED FIX (CLEAN & SAFE)


---

🧩 STEP 1: Create a Variable for Total Width

Instead of referencing controls, calculate width once.

In Screen → OnVisible:

Set(
    varTotalWidth,
    150 + 120 + (CountRows('SE Question List') * 110)
)


---

🧩 STEP 2: Use Variable Everywhere

HeaderContainer:

Width = varTotalWidth


---

Gallery_Suppliers:

Width = varTotalWidth


---

👉 Now NO circular reference ✅


---

🧠 WHY THIS WORKS

varTotalWidth = fixed calculation

Header → uses varTotalWidth  
Gallery → uses varTotalWidth  
(no dependency between controls)


